{
  "_about": "Pattern schemas per application, from Requirements/Application Patterns.xlsx (received 2026-11-02). A pattern name is <appId>:<prefix>:<field1>:...:<fieldN>. Each field: fieldLabel, regex (validate:match, whole value), hint, example, blankIsWildcard (blank becomes *). X:CLW keeps its own hand-built form and is not listed here. Judgement calls: X:BPMS(ASMT) prefix ORG (sheet says ORD, its example and Workday use ORG); X:OAM (sheet heading says X:OAMS, its example and Workday use X:OAM); X:SET and X:PHA have no organization type in Workday yet, so creating their patterns is refused until those types exist. Academic Unit is out of scope for now; Subject is checked by format because the tenant has no course-subject data source.",
